{
  "borough": "Harrow",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0cm; line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;The\r\nproposal, by reason of an unsatisfactory Flood Risk Assessment, fails to provide adequate flood data to demonstrate that the proposed development would result in a net reduction in\r\nflood risk, be resistant and resilient to flooding, would not exacerbate the\r\nrisk of flooding within the site or increase the risk and consequences of\r\nflooding elsewhere or provide a dry means of escape for the users of the site,\r\nto the potential detriment of the safety of future occupiers of the development\r\nand elsewhere in terms of flood risk.&amp;nbsp;\r\nThe proposed development would therefore be contrary to the National Planning Policy Framework (2023),&amp;nbsp;policy SI 12 of The London Plan (2021), Core Policy CS1 U of Harrow Core Strategy (2012) policies DM 9 and DM10 of the Harrow Development Management Polices Local Plan (2013).&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;margin: 0cm; line-height: normal;&quot;&gt;The\r\nproposed development, by reason of its awkward layout; poor outlook and lack of access to natural daylight/sunlight to the kitchen and dining area of the ground floor flat would result in a substandard\r\nquality of living accommodation for the potential future occupiers, to the\r\ndetriment of their residential amenity, contrary to the high quality design\r\naspirations of the National Planning Policy Framework (2023), Policy D6 of The\r\nLondon Plan (2021), policies DM1 and DM 26 of the Harrow Development Management\r\nPolicies Local Plan (2013), the Technical Housing Standards Nationally\r\nDescribed Space Standards (2015), the Mayor of London Supplementary Planning\r\nGuidance (2016) and the adopted Residential Design Guide Supplementary Planning\r\nDocument (2010).&lt;font face=&quot;Arial, sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
